 "result_text": "I changed `to_struct` in `stellar_sdk/scval.py` to sort the struct's fields alphabetically by name before building the map. I didn't run the repro script or any tests, so the fix is untested against the contract.\n\n**Cause (my inference):** the XDR in your report has the map keys in the order `source, asset, price, timestamp`. Soroban requires `ScMap` keys to be sorted, and symbol keys sort lexicographically. As far as I can tell, an unsorted map is what produces \"failed to convert ScVal to host value\". Rust sorts struct fields when it builds the map, so the Rust test passed.\n\n**Fix:** the same struct now serializes as `asset, price, source, timestamp`.\n\n**Not covered:** I didn't change `to_map`, so a map you build by hand still needs its keys in sorted order.",
